{"name":"Qing Dynasty Dragon","hex":"#4455ee","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"qing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sounding stone, a Chinese musical instrument."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/qing"},{"term":"dynasty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A series of rulers or dynasts from one family.","A family considered over time, with its ancestors and descendants"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dynasty"},{"term":"dragon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mythical reptilian or serpentine creature.","In European mythologies, a gigantic beast, typically reptilian with leathery bat-like wings, lion-like claws, scaly skin and a lizard-like body, often a monster with fiery breath."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of drag queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Qing dynasty","blocks":[{"text":"The Qing dynasty, officially the Great Qing, also known as the Qing Empire or Qing China, was a Manchu-led imperial dynasty of China and an early modern empire in East Asia which existed from 1636/1644 to 1912. The last imperial dynasty in Chinese history, the Qing dynasty was preceded by the Ming dynasty and succeeded by the Republic of China. At the height of its power, the empire stretched from the Sea of Japan in the east to the Pamir Mountains in the west, and from the Mongolian Plateau in the north to the South China Sea in the south. Originally emerging from the Later Jin dynasty founded in 1616 and proclaimed in Shenyang in 1636, the dynasty seized control of the Ming capital Beijing and North China in 1644, traditionally considered the start of the dynasty's rule. The dynasty lasted until the Xinhai Revolution of October 1911 led to the abdication of the last emperor in February 1912. The multi-ethnic Qing dynasty assembled the territorial base for modern China. The Qing controlled the most territory of any dynasty in Chinese history, and in 1790 was the fourth-largest empire in world history to that point. It was also the most populous state at the time, with over 426 million citizens in 1907."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Flag_of_China_%281889%E2%80%931912%29.svg/330px-Flag_of_China_%281889%E2%80%931912%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qing_dynasty"},{"title":"Dynasty","blocks":[{"text":"A dynasty is a sequence of rulers from the same family, usually in the context of a monarchical system, but sometimes also appearing in republics. A \"house\" is an imperial, royal or noble family, not always ruling. \nHistorians periodize the histories of many states and civilizations, such as the Roman Empire, Imperial Iran, Ancient Egypt (3100–30 BCE), and Ancient and Imperial China, using a framework of successive dynasties. As such, the term \"dynasty\" may be used to delimit the era during which a family reigned."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/The_Imperial_Family_of_Japan%2C_2021.jpg/330px-The_Imperial_Family_of_Japan%2C_2021.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynasty"},{"title":"Dragon","blocks":[{"text":"A dragon is a mythical creature found in the folklore of cultures throughout the world. It is roughly serpentine in form, and often possesses features drawn from different animals, such as wings and claws. In nearly all cultures, it is conceived of as a powerful and awe-inspiring creature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png/330px-St_Catherine%2C_St_George_and_the_Dragon_%28M%C3%A4staren_fr%C3%A5n_Kappenberg%29_-_Nationalmuseum_-_18337_%28brightened%29%2C_draken.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Minggunbattle.jpg/500px-Minggunbattle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Minggunbattle.jpg/500px-Minggunbattle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Manchu cavalry charging Ming infantry at the 1619 Battle of Sarhū","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMinggunbattle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Sura_han_ni_chiha._Currency_of_the_farther_East._No.850.jpg/500px-Sura_han_ni_chiha._Currency_of_the_farther_East._No.850.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Sura_han_ni_chiha._Currency_of_the_farther_East._No.850.jpg/500px-Sura_han_ni_chiha._Currency_of_the_farther_East._No.850.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Coins of Hong Taiji in Manchu script","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASura_han_ni_chiha._Currency_of_the_farther_East._No.850.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Dorgon%2C_the_Prince_Rui_%2817th_century%29.jpg/500px-Dorgon%2C_the_Prince_Rui_%2817th_century%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Dorgon%2C_the_Prince_Rui_%2817th_century%29.jpg/500px-Dorgon%2C_the_Prince_Rui_%2817th_century%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dorgon (1612–1650)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADorgon%2C_the_Prince_Rui_(17th_century).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Qing_Dynasty_1760.jpg/500px-Qing_Dynasty_